WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.800
Water never stays in one place.

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:07.620
The same water moves, again and again, between the sea, the sky and the land.

3
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.000
This journey is called the water cycle.

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:11.950
It begins with the sun.

5
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.670
Heat from the sun warms the surface of the sea,

6
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.100
and some of the water turns into an invisible gas: water vapour.

7
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.550
Plants give off water vapour from their leaves, too.

8
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.980
Warm, moist air rises.

9
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.760
As it rises, it cools, and the vapour turns back into tiny droplets of water.

10
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.420
Countless droplets together make a cloud.

11
00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.400
Inside the cloud, the droplets join and grow.

12
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.030
When they become too heavy to float, they fall as rain, or as snow where the air is cold.

13
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.690
On land, some of the water runs into streams and rivers.

14
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.900
Some soaks into the ground and is stored there.

15
00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.710
Sooner or later, most of it reaches the sea again.

16
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.410
And there, the sun warms it once more.

17
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.640
The cycle never stops.
